WEBVTT

00:03.160 --> 00:06.770
Fight for your justice,
show your courage.

00:06.770 --> 00:10.370
Right! Grasp truth in these hands.

00:10.370 --> 00:13.780
Fight for your justice, I want you

00:13.780 --> 00:21.200
as you fight through
with your head held up high.

00:35.860 --> 00:39.930
Rather than polishing diamonds

00:43.040 --> 00:46.970
give me a glistening future.

00:50.250 --> 00:52.480
Even if nothing's there, get up.

00:52.480 --> 00:56.350
It's important to turn on the switch.

00:57.450 --> 01:00.220
Something new that I don't want to yield.

01:00.220 --> 01:04.750
Seeking it is justice!

01:06.360 --> 01:09.930
Fight for your justice,
be serious about it.

01:09.930 --> 01:13.540
Right! Face reality head on.

01:13.540 --> 01:16.940
Fight for your justice,
I love how you

01:16.940 --> 01:27.340
never give up even if
the current is against you.

01:29.750 --> 01:32.490
The girl's name is Misty Cornwell.

01:32.490 --> 01:35.460
It says her age is 14.

01:35.460 --> 01:40.430
Correctly, 14 plus 63 years
of cold-sleep, ribbit!

01:40.430 --> 01:42.730
- Excuse me.
- She's the same as always.

01:43.830 --> 01:45.770
She's regained consciousness.

01:54.080 --> 01:55.340
What's that thing?

01:57.410 --> 01:58.850
It's all right, Q-chan.

01:58.850 --> 02:00.180
Don't...

02:00.180 --> 02:01.820
Cold...

02:01.820 --> 02:03.420
It's the effect of cold-sleep.

02:03.420 --> 02:06.390
You should rest for now.

02:06.390 --> 02:08.760
Wow, a handsome guy!

02:08.760 --> 02:09.720
Hey, hey.

02:09.720 --> 02:14.400
I heard you grew up in an environment
where men and women lived together.

02:14.400 --> 02:17.230
What nonsense are you talking about?

02:17.230 --> 02:18.600
Are you an idiot?

02:18.600 --> 02:20.260
I-Idiot?

02:23.070 --> 02:25.070
Hey, who is he?

02:25.070 --> 02:26.810
Who is "he"?

02:26.810 --> 02:28.980
Considering you're saying "he"...

02:28.980 --> 02:31.910
if it's not Bart,
then it would mean Hibiki.

02:31.910 --> 02:33.280
His name is Hibiki?

02:33.280 --> 02:35.350
How cute!

02:35.350 --> 02:39.390
I'm someone who believes
in love at first sight.

02:39.390 --> 02:42.860
You know, the red string of fate?

02:42.860 --> 02:47.330
Y-You... Stop saying
things that don't make sense!

02:47.330 --> 02:49.900
Being naive makes you cuter!

02:49.900 --> 02:51.070
- It's a heart!
- Come on...

02:51.070 --> 02:54.170
Don't stay there. Come close to me.

02:54.170 --> 02:55.900
N-No!

02:55.900 --> 02:59.530
First of all, red is
the color of bad aliens!

03:03.580 --> 03:06.050
The premonition of a battle... Pai-check!

03:13.620 --> 03:17.290
Hey, is that his girlfriend?

03:17.290 --> 03:18.630
Girlfriend?

03:18.630 --> 03:22.060
I'm not quite familiar
with that term's usage.

03:22.060 --> 03:24.800
What's up with that?
Are you serious when you say that?

03:24.800 --> 03:28.770
Q-chan, I think these
guys are all strange.

03:28.770 --> 03:30.440
It's the opposite.

03:30.440 --> 03:35.240
From our viewpoint,
you're strange as well.

03:35.240 --> 03:38.310
Where did I end up?

03:38.310 --> 03:43.320
We've grown up in an environment
where men and women live apart.

03:43.320 --> 03:45.490
I can't say which is more correct...

03:45.490 --> 03:49.320
but our views are quite different
from the ones you grew up with.

03:51.130 --> 03:55.560
But this definitely is strange.

03:55.560 --> 03:57.000
Here you go.

03:57.000 --> 04:00.740
That girl barges in...
And she's so selfish!

04:00.740 --> 04:04.640
But if you suddenly woke up
surrounded by unfamiliar people...

04:04.640 --> 04:06.440
I'm sure you'd be surprised.

04:06.440 --> 04:11.210
As soon as she woke up,
she hugged Mr. Alien!

04:11.210 --> 04:16.320
And Mr. Alien wasn't mad
like how he always is with me.

04:16.320 --> 04:17.550
Strange.

04:17.550 --> 04:19.650
It's somehow a little jolting.

04:22.660 --> 04:26.060
How's our guest doing?

04:26.060 --> 04:28.530
She's still asleep for now.

04:28.530 --> 04:31.100
Her vital functions are still unstable.

04:31.100 --> 04:34.240
Rest is the best
medicine for the time being.

04:34.240 --> 04:35.740
Then we have no choice.

04:35.740 --> 04:39.260
I guess we need to decode
this message on our own.

04:40.910 --> 04:43.810
I wish I didn't make that promise.

04:43.810 --> 04:47.220
Just waiting is boring.

04:47.220 --> 04:50.420
I want to chase after him like before.

04:50.420 --> 04:52.080
Dita...

04:54.890 --> 04:56.380
Ezra! What's wrong?

04:57.630 --> 04:59.690
The baby...

04:59.690 --> 05:02.290
The baby? It's about to be born?

05:03.160 --> 05:05.160
T-This is a huge problem!

05:06.270 --> 05:08.500
What's with that woman.

05:08.500 --> 05:10.670
Telling a guy that he's cute.

05:10.670 --> 05:13.170
Geez. Don't take me so lightly.

05:13.170 --> 05:15.310
Or so you say.

05:15.310 --> 05:17.310
You're smirking.

05:17.310 --> 05:20.980
I-I'm not smirking!

05:20.980 --> 05:24.590
Why don't you hurry up
and keep that promise?

05:24.590 --> 05:26.450
T-That's none of your business!

05:26.450 --> 05:29.360
Geez! You're all so damn annoying!

05:32.690 --> 05:34.160
This is no good.

05:35.930 --> 05:38.900
Geez, what did I do?

05:41.440 --> 05:44.410
Wait! Help me get to the doctor!

05:44.410 --> 05:46.430
Ezra's baby is about to be born!

05:47.880 --> 05:49.340
She's gone into labor?

05:50.380 --> 05:52.110
She looks like she's in a lot of pain!

05:52.110 --> 05:55.420
I'll take her right
over so you can look at her!

05:55.420 --> 05:58.690
Hibiki, can you explain
the situation in detail?

05:58.690 --> 05:59.950
What kind of pain?

05:59.950 --> 06:02.860
Will this really be all right?

06:07.800 --> 06:08.660
How is it?

06:08.660 --> 06:10.830
There's protection on it.

06:10.830 --> 06:15.740
To see the message,
we need some kind of password.

06:15.740 --> 06:17.210
Extra! Extra!

06:17.210 --> 06:19.410
Ezra's baby is about to be born!

06:19.410 --> 06:21.240
- What?
- That's a big problem!

06:21.240 --> 06:22.680
This is no time to...

06:22.680 --> 06:24.050
What are you saying?

06:24.050 --> 06:25.680
We're in the middle of work.

06:25.680 --> 06:27.010
But...

06:29.680 --> 06:30.840
Pyoro, what's wrong?

06:32.690 --> 06:34.290
What's this all of a sudden?

06:34.290 --> 06:36.690
It's having another tantrum?

06:39.530 --> 06:41.700
Wait, what's going on here?

06:41.700 --> 06:44.530
The entire ship's
systems have gone down!

06:44.530 --> 06:45.830
We can't control it!

06:45.830 --> 06:48.670
The contaminated area is
spreading at an alarming rate!

06:49.740 --> 06:53.570
To think there was
something set in that capsule.

06:57.210 --> 06:58.180
What?

06:58.180 --> 07:00.850
W-What's going on now?

07:00.850 --> 07:03.080
Hey, it stopped suddenly!

07:03.080 --> 07:04.090
What's going on?

07:04.090 --> 07:06.320
Hibiki, calm down and listen.

07:06.320 --> 07:08.920
We've had an unfortunate accident...

07:08.920 --> 07:11.460
and all power to the ship has ceased.

07:11.460 --> 07:14.020
I want to confirm the situation.
How is the patient doing?

07:15.760 --> 07:17.530
There's nothing to confirm!

07:17.530 --> 07:19.370
Just get us out of here quickly!

07:19.370 --> 07:21.300
She's in and out of pain.

07:21.300 --> 07:22.770
What's going on?

07:22.770 --> 07:24.440
That's labor.

07:24.440 --> 07:28.140
It's a sign that the baby
is ready to come outside.

07:29.980 --> 07:31.780
Both of you, listen up!

07:31.780 --> 07:33.250
Depending on the situation...

07:33.250 --> 07:36.280
in the worst case, you'll
have to deliver it right there!

07:36.280 --> 07:38.280
R-Right here?

07:39.990 --> 07:41.160
That's ridiculous!

07:41.160 --> 07:43.460
Then what are we going to do?

07:43.460 --> 07:45.980
The baby won't wait for us!

07:47.600 --> 07:49.760
It's all right, Ezra.

07:49.760 --> 07:52.470
You and the baby aren't alone.

07:52.470 --> 07:53.800
I'm here.

07:53.800 --> 07:55.640
Everyone else is, too.

07:55.640 --> 07:57.040
Mr. Alien is here, too.

07:58.970 --> 08:01.510
Y-Yeah.

08:01.510 --> 08:04.180
Thanks, Dita.

08:04.180 --> 08:05.410
Hibiki, too.

08:06.350 --> 08:08.420
Now, we've decided.

08:08.420 --> 08:10.580
What will we do next, Doctor?

08:13.250 --> 08:16.320
How far apart are the contractions?

08:16.320 --> 08:18.830
Hibiki, answer me.

08:18.830 --> 08:23.430
They're much closer
than before, but now...

08:23.430 --> 08:24.990
Dita, it's here!

08:26.930 --> 08:30.170
When there are more than
6 contractions in an hour...

08:32.410 --> 08:34.110
What now?

08:34.110 --> 08:35.870
At a time like this...

08:42.220 --> 08:44.350
We couldn't use the
radar with the system down!

08:44.350 --> 08:45.920
We didn't spot them in time!

08:45.920 --> 08:48.090
Enemy forces are approaching!

08:48.090 --> 08:52.260
With the Paksis failing,
we can't raise the Nirvana's shields!

08:52.260 --> 08:54.960
Gascogne! Can we use the Dreads?

08:54.960 --> 08:56.330
Of course!

08:56.330 --> 09:00.600
Leave the outfielders to us,
and get rid of the virus quickly.

09:01.970 --> 09:03.230
I'm trying my best.

09:04.370 --> 09:06.770
Well, everyone. Give it what ya got.

09:06.770 --> 09:09.580
It's your chance to unload
your stress through exercise.

09:09.580 --> 09:14.480
We've got to turn all the extra
energy towards the toppings, right?

09:15.780 --> 09:18.290
What? Nobody's here?

09:18.290 --> 09:20.620
Sorry, we've got our hands full.

09:20.620 --> 09:23.960
The orders went through though,
so go on your own.

09:23.960 --> 09:25.430
We've got no choice for now.

09:25.430 --> 09:26.420
Let's go, girls!

09:38.370 --> 09:40.100
Barnette, going out!

09:46.650 --> 09:48.620
The Nirvana is malfunctioning.

09:48.620 --> 09:50.990
We'll go with attack pattern delta-4!

09:50.990 --> 09:51.720
Roger!

09:51.720 --> 09:56.120
Geez! I wanted to see where
the baby was being delivered!

09:56.120 --> 09:57.110
They're coming!

10:02.830 --> 10:04.200
Ezra, hold on!

10:04.200 --> 10:05.470
She's still in pain!

10:05.470 --> 10:07.130
What should we do?

10:10.570 --> 10:13.940
How long are you
going to act so confused?

10:13.940 --> 10:20.620
I don't know what the action of
"straining to widen the birth canal" is.

10:20.620 --> 10:23.080
All right, I get it.

10:23.080 --> 10:28.820
You know, Doctor, there are times
when experience wins over logic.

10:28.820 --> 10:29.590
However...

10:29.590 --> 10:31.530
It's all right. Just leave it to me.

10:31.530 --> 10:33.490
Ezra! Can you hear me?

10:33.490 --> 10:34.930
Don't push just yet!

10:34.930 --> 10:37.230
Use shallow breaths
to help ease the pain.

10:37.230 --> 10:38.220
Right.

10:51.550 --> 10:52.530
Ezra!

10:54.980 --> 10:56.450
Mr. Alien!

10:56.450 --> 10:59.210
See, men can be useful.

11:03.020 --> 11:04.930
- What?
- What's wrong, Hibiki?

11:04.930 --> 11:07.800
Water! There's water!

11:07.800 --> 11:11.030
Calm down, that's
just the water breaking.

11:11.030 --> 11:15.600
The amniotic fluid protecting the
baby inside the womb is spilling out.

11:15.600 --> 11:19.810
Without that, the baby would not
easily make it through the birth canal.

11:19.810 --> 11:21.880
It's an important function.

11:21.880 --> 11:24.340
I have no idea what you're talking about.

11:26.710 --> 11:29.180
Enemy flagships approaching
from both sides!

11:31.820 --> 11:33.690
What?

11:33.690 --> 11:36.050
What are they up to?

11:44.800 --> 11:47.130
I'm glad I wasn't inside.

11:47.130 --> 11:48.100
You're useless.

11:51.610 --> 11:56.040
Damn it, if I could go out,
I'd finish the enemy in a hurry.

11:56.040 --> 11:59.480
Mr. Alien, think about
Ezra and the baby for now!

11:59.480 --> 12:00.680
You say that, but...

12:00.680 --> 12:02.840
Don't, both of you.

12:04.720 --> 12:08.090
Hibiki and Dita...

12:08.090 --> 12:10.290
You two should be friendly.

12:10.290 --> 12:11.950
Okay?

12:18.930 --> 12:21.340
O-Old hag, she's in pain again!

12:21.340 --> 12:22.640
What should I do?

12:22.640 --> 12:23.940
It's finally on its way!

12:23.940 --> 12:25.840
Who's closer to her legs?

12:27.040 --> 12:28.180
That would be me!

12:28.180 --> 12:29.580
Then you do it, boy!

12:29.580 --> 12:33.980
Spread her legs, and when the baby's
head comes out, help it outside.

12:33.980 --> 12:35.640
Help it?

12:36.850 --> 12:38.950
Please, Mr. Alien!

12:38.950 --> 12:41.420
- Ezra, are you ready?
- Yeah!

12:43.820 --> 12:46.190
A-All right, I've come around!

12:46.190 --> 12:48.160
Then push, Ezra.

12:48.160 --> 12:49.830
Gather your breath.

12:49.830 --> 12:52.130
One, two, three, push!

12:57.870 --> 13:00.170
H-Head! The head is showing!

13:00.170 --> 13:02.940
Really, Mr. Alien?

13:02.940 --> 13:05.550
Just a little more! Push!

13:05.550 --> 13:08.150
Hibiki, it's almost delivered.

13:08.150 --> 13:10.080
You'll see it come out soon.

13:10.080 --> 13:12.120
Calm down and pull the baby out.

13:12.120 --> 13:13.750
Don't make it sound so easy!

13:13.750 --> 13:15.560
Please, Mr. Alien!

13:15.560 --> 13:17.690
I can't. I have no strength left.

13:17.690 --> 13:20.260
Get a grip! You're a guy, right?

13:20.260 --> 13:22.200
This is one thing I can't stand!

13:22.200 --> 13:23.800
Then I'll do it!

13:23.800 --> 13:26.130
Mr. Alien, you support Ezra!

13:26.130 --> 13:28.000
Dita...

13:28.000 --> 13:31.740
Your baby is something
we've all looked forward to.

13:31.740 --> 13:37.550
That's why we definitely,
definitely want a safe delivery!

13:37.550 --> 13:39.250
Dita...

13:39.250 --> 13:40.910
Thank you.

13:42.950 --> 13:46.290
Oh? What's with the change in attitude?

13:46.290 --> 13:48.360
I finally understand.

13:48.360 --> 13:51.980
You don't need a textbook
for the birth of a new life.

13:54.030 --> 13:56.460
Ezra, you'll be all right now.

13:56.460 --> 13:58.670
The head is coming out properly.

13:58.670 --> 14:01.000
You'll see the baby soon enough, Ezra!

14:04.510 --> 14:05.710
W-What should we do?

14:05.710 --> 14:07.740
At this rate,
they'll take us ship and all!

14:07.740 --> 14:10.610
You say that, but what can we do?

14:10.610 --> 14:12.200
Sheesh, he's so...

14:14.680 --> 14:17.380
Aim for the device shot into the Nirvana.

14:17.380 --> 14:19.290
Jura and Barnette, the left's yours.

14:19.290 --> 14:20.280
- Roger!
- Roger!

14:22.390 --> 14:25.230
Captain! Most of the
head is showing through now!

14:25.230 --> 14:26.930
Don't push anymore!

14:26.930 --> 14:28.730
Start the shallow breaths again.

14:28.730 --> 14:31.430
Dita, slowly reach in
and support the baby.

14:31.430 --> 14:32.420
Okay!

14:38.070 --> 14:39.400
Just a bit more!

14:47.250 --> 14:48.720
This voice...

14:48.720 --> 14:49.680
That's right.

14:49.680 --> 14:52.620
Another life has been
born into this world.

14:54.290 --> 14:56.450
I wanted to see it, too.

14:58.860 --> 15:00.530
It's born, Ezra!

15:00.530 --> 15:01.560
Amazing...

15:01.560 --> 15:04.550
This is... a baby...

15:05.670 --> 15:06.630
Mr. Alien?

15:06.630 --> 15:08.170
Are you all right?

15:08.170 --> 15:09.670
Mr. Alien!

15:09.670 --> 15:12.740
A spineless boy till the very end.

15:12.740 --> 15:14.340
A job well done, Ezra.

15:14.340 --> 15:16.980
And you too, Dita!

15:16.980 --> 15:17.970
This voice...

15:24.850 --> 15:27.050
This is annoying! You're in my way!

15:38.430 --> 15:40.830
Hey, guys! The baby is born!

15:40.830 --> 15:42.440
Really?

15:42.440 --> 15:43.600
I'm so glad.

15:47.840 --> 15:50.000
Ezra, congratulations.

15:55.350 --> 15:56.950
This is...

15:56.950 --> 15:58.020
Where is this?

15:58.020 --> 16:00.220
Who am I?

16:00.220 --> 16:01.490
What is this voice?

16:01.490 --> 16:02.760
The voice of a baby?

16:02.760 --> 16:03.890
Pyoro-2's voice?

16:03.890 --> 16:07.090
I can't stay here!

16:07.090 --> 16:11.230
But to think that the baby's
voice was the password.

16:11.230 --> 16:13.370
The system is reviving.

16:13.370 --> 16:16.430
The Paksis has returned to normal.

16:21.610 --> 16:25.080
She's already sound asleep.

16:25.080 --> 16:26.910
I'm sure she felt safe.

16:26.910 --> 16:29.550
Thank you for waiting!

16:29.550 --> 16:31.350
Sorry, I'll move you right now.

16:31.350 --> 16:32.720
Please, hurry.

16:32.720 --> 16:34.380
Roger!

16:38.430 --> 16:40.950
Idiot! What are you doing dropping us?

16:43.360 --> 16:44.630
Pyoro-2...

16:44.630 --> 16:47.330
I'll protect Pyoro-2!

16:50.100 --> 16:52.440
Too many stimuli...

16:55.910 --> 16:59.210
The sender, to differentiate
between enemies and allies...

16:59.210 --> 17:04.180
used a certain voice pulse as the
password to unlock the protection.

17:04.180 --> 17:07.190
And what was that password?

17:07.190 --> 17:08.590
The voice of a baby.

17:08.590 --> 17:09.660
What was that?

17:09.660 --> 17:14.060
Strangely enough,
Ezra's child saved us all.

17:14.060 --> 17:18.230
Does that mean that there
are no more babies on Earth?

17:18.230 --> 17:21.040
Or that they can no longer be born.

17:21.040 --> 17:23.800
It's faster to check what's inside.

17:23.800 --> 17:24.670
BC.

17:24.670 --> 17:25.660
Roger.

17:29.280 --> 17:33.980
I apologize for putting such
a cumbersome trap on this message.

17:33.980 --> 17:37.220
We believed that the sound
of a new life being born...

17:37.220 --> 17:40.590
was the sign of
healthy human prosperity.

17:40.590 --> 17:42.820
Those that have
accepted this message...

17:42.820 --> 17:47.760
I hope, are undergoing human
life as it was meant to be.

17:47.760 --> 17:53.800
Things have drastically changed
since you left your homeland of Earth.

17:53.800 --> 17:56.940
After we saw you off in
the fleet of frontier ships...

17:56.940 --> 18:02.010
madness overtook Earth when the
further prosperity of man was hoped for.

18:02.010 --> 18:03.440
As you may know...

18:03.440 --> 18:08.050
humans have reached a saturation
in their genetic distribution rate.

18:08.050 --> 18:10.320
In other words, as long
as we remain on Earth...

18:10.320 --> 18:13.550
we have lost the possibility of evolution.

18:13.550 --> 18:15.560
For further evolution...

18:15.560 --> 18:19.890
people had supposedly
chosen to travel outside Earth.

18:19.890 --> 18:21.330
However...

18:21.330 --> 18:23.300
Take a look at this.

18:23.300 --> 18:26.300
This is what your beautiful
homeland looks like now.

18:26.300 --> 18:32.240
The once blue atmosphere has been
covered by ugly gears like a cage...

18:32.240 --> 18:35.840
and it forcibly pulled
in the moon, its satellite.

18:35.840 --> 18:39.350
As a result, Earth suffered a drastic
change in gravitational force...

18:39.350 --> 18:41.380
and the atmosphere is a chronic storm.

18:41.380 --> 18:45.490
The surface is now like
a giant washing machine.

18:45.490 --> 18:47.450
What few Earthlings are left...

18:47.450 --> 18:52.990
have created cities within these gears,
and hold on for dear life.

18:52.990 --> 18:56.860
They, who had seen you off with the hope
of mankind, have started to believe...

18:56.860 --> 19:02.500
perhaps out of loneliness,
that they are the only pure humans.

19:02.500 --> 19:07.040
They have started to believe in
the old idea of self-preservation.

19:07.040 --> 19:10.510
However, because they have lost
all possibility of evolution...

19:10.510 --> 19:12.950
cloning does not work well, either.

19:12.950 --> 19:14.480
That is when, of all things...

19:14.480 --> 19:17.480
They claimed your organs that
survived perilous environments...

19:17.480 --> 19:21.120
as ingredients for self-preservation!

19:21.120 --> 19:23.520
So that's what the harvest is all about.

19:23.520 --> 19:27.660
I don't know why they suddenly
turned towards this madness.

19:27.660 --> 19:31.800
But they used the
one original Paksis left...

19:31.800 --> 19:34.300
and created an automatic
fleet of harvesters...

19:34.300 --> 19:37.830
to completely and
mercilessly harvest you all.

19:39.440 --> 19:42.810
The choice that Earth
has made is clearly mistaken.

19:42.810 --> 19:48.050
To stop this insanity,
we are sending a messenger.

19:48.050 --> 19:50.620
I don't know when and where we will meet.

19:50.620 --> 19:54.990
But to regain the stature of humans
as we were originally meant to be...

19:54.990 --> 19:59.960
and to protect the circle of
life that we pass on and entrust...

19:59.960 --> 20:02.700
If you are watching this message...

20:02.700 --> 20:07.600
please stand up, so that you
don't extinguish the fire of life.

20:09.370 --> 20:12.340
To protect the circle of life...

20:12.340 --> 20:14.840
We've definitely accepted this message.

20:14.840 --> 20:17.440
Let's inherit their feelings.

20:17.440 --> 20:21.280
For a world where that child
can grow up with smiles.

20:22.580 --> 20:24.820
So cute...

20:24.820 --> 20:27.620
Hey, Ezra. Have you decided on a name yet?

20:27.620 --> 20:28.860
Pyoro-2!

20:28.860 --> 20:31.960
No way! That's not cute at all!

20:31.960 --> 20:33.730
This has already been decided!

20:33.730 --> 20:35.960
That's right! We can have
the captain decide the name!

20:35.960 --> 20:36.760
Pyoro-2!

20:36.760 --> 20:38.420
- Pyoro-2!
- Oh?

20:40.130 --> 20:42.640
Are you all right already?

20:42.640 --> 20:44.200
Yeah, I'm perfectly fine.

20:44.200 --> 20:46.010
Congratulations on the baby.

20:46.010 --> 20:47.670
Thank you.

20:50.110 --> 20:51.310
Mr. Alien!

20:51.310 --> 20:53.050
What is it now?

20:53.050 --> 20:55.980
Oh, um, sorry.

20:55.980 --> 20:57.880
Oh, it's all right.

20:57.880 --> 21:00.490
That's right! Hurry up and
take a look at the baby!

21:00.490 --> 21:01.750
I heard!

21:03.360 --> 21:06.490
You passed out after
one look at the baby?

21:06.490 --> 21:08.630
What? Are you mocking me?

21:08.630 --> 21:11.890
I love people like that!

21:16.140 --> 21:17.800
He's so cute!

21:21.070 --> 21:22.740
Pai-check!

21:24.540 --> 21:26.480
A premonition to a battle!
